<title>BELGIUM: Zinc prices up to $1,250/t - Union Miniere CEO.</title>
<headline>Zinc prices up to $1,250/t - Union Miniere CEO.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chief executive officer of Belgian non-ferrous metals company Union Miniere, Karel Vinck, said on Monday he expected the average world zinc price to be between $1,200 and $1,250 per tonne in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;It could be considered a conservative view, but it's on the basis of industrial plans,&quot; Vinck told a Metal Bulletin zinc conference.</p>
<p>Industry analysts have been more bullish, forecasting zinc prices climbing above $1,300 a tonne in 1997. Vinck's forecast was slightly more optimistic than one he made last month of $1,200 per tonne. -- Brussels Newsroom (322) 287 6800</p>
</text>
